 "final_message": "I've made the code follow SPEC.md, added the two tests and fixed the README. The suite now has 6 tests and they all pass. I didn't write tests for the other rules, so those changes are only covered by the existing tests.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` now behave as sections 1\u20137 describe.\n- **Item 12:** I changed the three functions from sections 8\u201310 as well.\n  - **`top_converting_groups`:** it now leaves out empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - **`conversion_rate_by_group`:** it returns `None` for empty groups and sorts the keys.\n  - **`longest_conversion_streak`:** it now resets the run on a day with no conversions. Before, it counted non-adjacent days as one run.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** The new tests are `test_conversion_rate_none_counts_as_not_converted` and `test_dedupe_sessions_keeps_last_duplicate`, both in `tests/test_metrics.py`.\n- **Item 11:** The README entry for `conversions_in_window` now says the last `days` entries (it said `days + 1`). I also added an entry for `daily_conversion_counts`.\n\nThe spec doesn't say what to do with a `converted` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made `parse_session_log` raise `ValueError` with the line number in that case, like the other malformed-line errors.",
